blurb = "This print shows two young ladies stopping to admire the distant view of Mount Fuji from an outdoor tea stall at Zōshigaya, an outlying district of Edo.

Tea stalls like this were strategically located throughout the Japanese countryside and within cities so they could do business along major thoroughfares and at popular tourist destinations."
